<!--
  Audio versions of endjin blog posts, published as a Podcasting 2.0 feed.

  Authored rather than mirrored: endjin publishes audio versions of some posts under
  /assets/podcast/, but no podcast RSS feed of its own, so this file assembles real assets into the
  feed a podcast host would serve. The enclosure URL, its media type and its byte count are real.

  The namespace is https://podcastindex.org/namespace/1.0 — https, and matched exactly. A feed
  declaring the http:// form silently yields no extension at all, because discovery compares the
  namespace URI rather than the prefix.

  The podcast:txt element with purpose="applepodcastsverify" is the reason this extension matters. A
  survey of live feeds found the Apple ownership token delivered that way by 21 publishers and as
  itunes:applepodcastsverify by 26, so a library reading only the iTunes form serves about half of
  the publishers who set one, and loses the other half's claim to their own show.
-->
